title: LilGuy_Respite
---
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
<<expression Nubs neutral>>
Luna: <i>His electric eyes wander and become mesmerized by the sky's dusky colors.</i>
<<if visited("Bad_Outcome") == true>>
Nubs: Today is still better than all the other days I have lived in the lab.
<<endif>>
<<if visited("Bad_Outcome") == false>>
<<expression Nubs arms_happy>>
Nubs: Today is the best day ever.
<<endif>>
<<declare $lilday = 0>>
<<jump LilGuy_Day>>
===

title: LilGuy_Day
---
-> What are your days usually like? <<once>>
    <<set $lilday += 1>>
    Nubs: Undergoing 20-30 tests a day to assess my durability. As the greatest product ever developed by AGENTS, I need to withstand drowning, poison, plasma, and firestorms. 
    <<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
    Nubs: In case the place I am stored in explodes from an incoming stealth missile.
    Nubs: Then I get squeezed back into a capsule that is smaller than the pod you freed me from.
    <<expression Nubs worried>>
    Nubs: It was kinda hard to breathe in there, now that I think about it.
    <<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
    Luna: That’s inhumane. Isn’t this against a law or something?
    <<expression Nubs loading>>
    Nubs: Title XVI, Section 23, Clause 8: It is not considered worker or animal cruelty if the organism was not constructed with a bladder.
    <<expression Nubs neutral>>
    Nubs: I do not have one. So I suppose there really is no logical reason for me to leave my capsule, after all.    
    <<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
    Luna: What a convenient loophole…
    <<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
    <<jump LilGuy_Day>>
-> What made today so great? <<once>>
    <<set $lilday += 1>>
    Nubs: Meeting you. And getting to see how humans live.
    // If player’s $badend score is >= 5, then show this line of text and expression below:
    <<if $badend >= 5>>
        <<expression Nubs angry>>
        Nubs: Even if you are intolerable and inhospitable at times…
        <<expression Nubs neutral>>
    <<else>>
    // If player’s $badend score is <=4, then continue with the below:
        Nubs: You have a good life.
        <<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
        Luna: Don't bullshit me.
        Luna: There's nothing “good” about my life at all.
        Nubs: You do not have to be poked and stuffed into a capsule, only for the same thing to happen to you the next day. You can do whatever you want, with unrestricted access to the city.
        <<expression Nubs happy>>
        Nubs: And you’ll use that access to take me back to my master, which you promised you would do once we completed this delivery!
        Luna: …
        <<expression Nubs neutral>>
        Nubs: You are not a prototype. You are…an original. 
        <<expression Nubs worried>>
        Nubs: At least you have a purpose…
    <<endif>>
// When the two questions above have been played through, reveal this choice to continue with the main story:
<<if $lilday == 2>>
    -> What is your purpose?
        Luna: So what is your purpose? Why were YOU created?
        <<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
        Luna: And don't give me that firewall crap.
        <<expression Nubs confused>>
        Nubs: But, I really cannot access those files…
        Luna: Then what do YOU want your purpose to be?
        <<expression Nubs neutral>>
        Nubs: …!
        Luna: Okay, so you can't access it. So what? What do YOU want to do?
        <<expression Nubs arms_worried>>
        Luna: <i>Nubs is genuinely stumped by my question. Nothing in his database is able to retrieve a clear answer.</i>
        <<expression Luna_Neutral shy_neutral>>
        Luna: I know I'm supposed to drop you off at your master's, but…it doesn't seem like you even wanna go back to pokes and firestorms.
        Luna: You…deserve to live…        
        <<expression Nubs neutral>>
        Nubs: Luna…
        <<expression Luna_Neutral shy>>
        Luna: (Ugh, why am I even saying this? It's like I'm trying to give myself a pep talk.)
        // Stop music
        <<stopMusic>>
        <<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
        <<expression Nubs arms_neutral>>
        ???: You deserve JAIL TIME.
<<endif>>
<<pose Luna_Neutral SceneSample_LunaFadeOut>>
<<pose Nubs SceneSample_NubsFadeOut>>
<<wait 1>>
<<exit Luna_Neutral>>
<<exit Nubs>>
<<fadeOut 1>>
<<jump MaxxIntro>>
===

title: MaxxIntro
---
// Play JunkYard music track
<<playMusic junkyard>>
<<camera Bridge>>
<<fadeIn 1>>
<<place Luna_Neutral>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
<<place CompanionNubs>>
<<expression CompanionNubs arms_neutral>>
<<place Maxx>>
<<expression Maxx neutral>>
<<wait 1>>
???: Straight to jail.
<<expression Luna_Neutral arms_annoyed>>
Luna: <i>A douchebag with an augmented glass jaw rolls up next to me on his bulky motorbike. The thing has been customized to bits to show off—and not to drive.</i>
Luna: <i>I press my weight deeper into my motorbike, ready to bounce at any moment.</i>
Luna: Who the hell are you?
<<expression Maxx intrigued>>
Maxx: The one true ascended adonis of AGENTS, Maxx.
Maxx: Lanklets refer to me as their Chief Product Officer, but our elevated CEO prefers the new-age term “Disciple” for his executive C-suite.
<<expression CompanionNubs wave_neutral>>
Nubs: That's the guy who named me T.A.B!
Luna: …Makes sense.
<<expression CompanionNubs arms_neutral>>
<<expression Maxx neutral>>
Maxx: I finally found you after combing through AGENTS highway footage.
Maxx: You've been driving around town with company property. 
<<expression CompanionNubs arms_worried>>
Nubs: …
Maxx: If you're a smart girl, you'll hand over that pillbug and continue on with your extremely jester life.
<<expression CompanionNubs arms_worried>>

-> Over your gigachad body.
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<expression Maxx intrigued>>
    Maxx: Flame me all you want, but everyone wishes they had my body and brain chemistry.
    Maxx: My jaw is made from Area 27 diamonds. No amount of mewing and semaglutides could ever get to my level.
-> And what do I get in return for handing him over?
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <<expression Maxx intrigued>>
    Maxx: Good strategy! I admire your business mindset.
    Maxx: But the only ROI you'll get is a life behind bars for stealing AGENTS property!
-> And if I don't?
    Maxx: A life behind bars for stealing AGENTS property!
<<jump MaxxThreat>>
===

title: MaxxThreat
---
Nubs: …
<<expression Maxx intrigued>>
Maxx: Don't act innocent, little pillbug. I overheard your non-compliant conversation with the girl.
Maxx: You, having a life of your own?
Maxx: Once I take you back, you'll be torn apart for the next prototype! Though given your recent acts of sacrilege, I doubt we'll salvage anything from your existing parts.
<<expression Maxx neutral>>
Maxx: As for you.
Luna: <i>His glass jaw glows as his internal system scans me and my motorbike over.</i>
Maxx: Let’s see here…
Maxx: A fake license plate. Multiple accounts of speeding. And stealing intellectual property from an AGENTS lab.
Luna: (He’s confusing me with the person who stole Nubs from the lab…)
Maxx: Not only will I suspend your SL0P account, but I’ll also process a warrant for your arrest and assign a CENTURY’S worth of debt to your bank account!
<<expression Luna_Neutral shy_annoyed>>
Luna: (Shit, I'm already swimming in debt! I can't afford any more…!)
Maxx: Buuuuut if you let the pillbug go now, I GUESS I'll let you and your busted bike continue to use the SL0P app.
<<expression Maxx intrigued>>
Maxx: And, as an add-on, I'll drop the debt charges. Because I'm SUCH a forgiving god.
<<expression CompanionNubs arms_worried>>
Nubs: …
<<expression Luna_Neutral shy_neutral>>
Luna: (This might be my last chance to bargain…)
<<jump MaxxChoices>>
===

title: MaxxChoices
---
-> Take the deal.
    <<jump BadEnding1>>
-> Don't take the deal.
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    Luna: (Do it scared. Even if it fucks me over.)
    <<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
    <<expression CompanionNubs arms_neutral>>
    Luna: No deal. I'm keeping him. And his name’s Nubs.
    <<expression Maxx annoyed>>
    Maxx: WHAT? Are you stupid!?
    Nubs: L-Luna! But why—?
    <<expression Nubs wave_worried>>
    Nubs: Ah!
    Luna: <i>I scoop him up and ram my foot on my motorbike’s pedal.</i>
    Luna: If you want him, then you're gonna have to get him!
    // Motorcycle SFX sound
    <<playSFX lunaMotorcycle>>
    Luna: <i>And with that, I start hauling ass back to Root Town.</i>
    <<pose Luna_Neutral SceneSample_LunaFadeOut>>
    <<pose CompanionNubs SceneSample_CompanionNubsFadeOut>>
    <<wait 1>> 
    <<exit Luna_Neutral>>
    <<exit CompanionNubs>>
-> Tell him you're not the person he's looking for. <<once>>
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
    Luna: None of this is my fault—because someone else gave me this task. THAT’S the real person you're after.
    Maxx: Doesn't matter. You still unlocked AGENTS-sanctioned property and that's against SL0P app policy.
    <<expression Maxx intrigued>>
    Maxx: And thanks for the tip! I'll make sure to lock BOTH of you up!
    <<expression Luna_Neutral arms_annoyed>>
    Luna: (Shit, that didn't work.)
    Nubs: Luna…
    <<jump MaxxChoices>>
-> Flirt and distract him before you make a run for it.
    <<expression Maxx intrigued>>
    Maxx: Thanks, but you're not my type.
    <<pose Luna_Neutral SceneSample_LunaFadeOut>>
    <<pose CompanionNubs SceneSample_CompanionNubsFadeOut>>
    <<wait 1>>
    <<exit Luna_Neutral>>
    <<exit CompanionNubs>>
    Maxx: Refusing women, sports, and beer are what separate me from the average man who’s ladaring. Dating would keep me from being my one true, elevated self.
    Maxx: And there's no ROI in love.
    <<expression Maxx neutral>>
    Maxx: …
    <<expression Maxx annoyed>>
    Maxx: Tch!
    Luna: <i>The dumbass was so into himself, making it easy for me and Nubs to escape and leave him in the dust.</i>
    Luna: <i>I was already hauling my ass back to Root Town.</i>

<<expression Maxx annoyed>>
Maxx: Well played. But it’s not over.
Maxx: Didn't think I'd need to use this…
// Stop Junk Yard music track
<<stopMusic>>
// Play Beep SFX
<<playSFX beep>>
<<exit Maxx>>
<<fadeOut 1>>
<<jump LilGuyBrainwashed>>
===


title: BadEnding1
---
Luna: (The stakes are too high. I don't want to owe anyone anything. Not anymore.)
<<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
<<expression SceneSampleEvents CompanionNubs arms_worried>>
Luna: Fine.
<<expression Maxx intrigued>>
<<expression CompanionNubs wave_worried>>
Nubs: L-Luna, no!
Luna: <i>I toss Nubs over to the overgrown gigachad. The creature is just a prototype, after all.</i>
Maxx: Smart girl. I knew you'd make the right choice.
Nubs: N-No…!
Maxx: To the scrapyard, pillbug!
// Play Beep SFX
<<playSFX beep>>
<<expression CompanionNubs wave_neutral>>
Nubs: !!!
<<expression CompanionNubs agents>>
Nubs: …
<<pose CompanionNubs SceneSample_CompanionNubsFadeOut>>
<<pose Maxx SceneSample_MaxxFadeOut>>
<<wait 1>>
<<exit Maxx>>
<<exit CompanionNubs>>
Luna: <i>I block out the gigachad's cackling as he rides away with the city’s most dangerous weapon.</i> 
Luna: <i>I sigh, turning to look at Frisscity’s glistening cityscape one last time before I ride off as if nothing ever happened.</i>
Luna: <i>Because nothing did.</i>
Luna: <i>Tonight was just another night of trying to survive.</i>
<<pose Luna_Neutral SceneSample_LunaFadeOut>>
<<wait 1>>
<<exit Luna_Neutral>>
<<stopMusic>>
<<fadeOut 2>>
// Show a screen with BAD END image
<<camera BadEnd>>
// Play the Error of Our Ways music track
<<playMusic endingTheme>>
<<fadeIn 2>>
<<wait 5>>
<<fadeOut 2>>
/////////// Create a command to automatically return to the Title Screen
===


title: LilGuyBrainwashed
---
// Play Deadroom track
<<playMusic deadroom>>
// Show the Bridge environment bridge asset, TBD if we’ll have an on the bridge background asset or not!
<<camera Bridge>>
<<fadeIn 2>>
<<wait 1>>
Luna: <i>I speed my way onto The Bridge, weaving around self-driving cars and corporate megabuses that shuttle underpaid workers back home.</i>
Luna: <i>It's just a few more miles before I reach Root Town, where Frisscity's high-tech gadgets lose signal—and hold no power over me.</i>
<<place Luna_Neutral>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
<<place CompanionNubs>>
<<expression CompanionNubs agents>>
Nubs: …
Luna: W-What the hell?!
Luna: Nubs!? Hey! Wake up!
Luna: <i>A hypnotic swirl dominates Nubs's screenface. His body freezes in place, clinging onto the nape of my neck as I race past another bus.</i>
Luna: <i>The more I stare at the spiral, the more I feel…enticed by it.</i>
Luna: <i>I quickly blink the sensation away, shaking my head and turning back to the road I’m racing down.</i>
Luna: (I can’t look at that thing. It’s like it’s drilling a hole into my mind…)
Luna: <i>Suddenly, a new voice takes over Nubs.</i>
// Do NOT call Maxx’s sprite to appear
Maxx: There you are.
<<expression Luna_Neutral annoyed>>
Luna: (Shit, he can track me…?!)
// Play SFX Maxx motorcycle sound
<<playSFX maxxMotorcycle>>
A motor mixed with ego and neon particles roars behind me in the distance.
Maxx: Won't be long before I catch up. 
Luna: <i>My breath stalls. Sweat starts beading at the back of my neck.</i>
Luna: (I knew there was a cost to shoving it to AGENTS and that overgrown gigachad.)
Luna: (But I'm totally fucking screwed!)
Luna: (Was this choice even worth it…?!)
<<jump Cybergulls>>
===


title: Cybergulls
---
// Play SFX Cybergull M 
<<playSFX caws>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
Luna: !!!
Luna: <i>The squawk of a cybergull splits the sky. I look up, keeping my foot on the accelerator.</i>
<<if $withCog == true>>
// Enter Cybergull with cog on
<<place CyberSeagull>>
<<expression CyberSeagull cog>>
Luna: (It’s that gull from the dumpster…)
Luna: (He thugged it out and now he’s able to fly with that cog…)
<<endif>>
<<if $withCog == false>>
// Enter Cybergull without the cog on
<<place CyberSeagull>>
<<expression CyberSeagull cogless>>
Luna: (It’s that gull from the dumpster…)
<<endif>>
// SFX Cybergull S 
<<playSFX caw>>
Luna: <i>He lets out another loud, electrifying battle cry that rings out across The Bridge.</i>
// Exit Cybergull
<<pose CyberSeagull SceneSample_CybergullFadeOut>>
<<wait 1>>
<<exit CyberSeagull>>
Luna: <i>Shadows materialize in the distance, and I begin to see a whole horde of cybergulls flap towards us.</i>
Luna: (HE’S A GANG LEADER?!?!)
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
Luna: (Wait…)
Luna: <i>The Bridge is a prime roost for cybergulls, who love to swoop down and swipe whatever shines the brightest.</i>
Luna: (This could actually be my key to ditching Maxx for good!)
// Play SFX Maxx motorcycle sound
<<playSFX maxxMotorcycle>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
<<place Maxx>>
<<expression Maxx intrigued>>
Luna: <i>Suddenly I hear tires screeching and then, in a blink of an eye, I see Maxx riding right beside me on his shining stallion of iron garbage.</i>
Maxx: Boo.
<<expression Luna_Neutral annoyed>>
Luna: …
Luna: <i>We're both speeding down the road, neck and neck.</i>
<<expression Maxx annoyed>>
Maxx: Why aren’t you pulling over? I GOT you. You’re going to JAIL!
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
Luna: Not yet.
// SFX motorcycle tires
<<playSFX tiresScreech>>
<<pose Luna_Neutral SceneSample_LunaFadeOut>>
<<pose CompanionNubs SceneSample_CompanionNubsFadeOut>>
<<wait 1>>
<<exit Luna_Neutral>>
<<exit CompanionNubs>>
Luna: <i>I veer off, making a hard left turn onto another highway onramp. It's the turn only a Root Town local would know.</i>
Maxx: Dammit!
Luna: <i>Maxx doesn't make the turn in time and continues straight…right into the growing horde of cybergulls.</i>
<<exit Maxx>>
<<fadeOut 2>>
<<jump Cybergull_CG>>
===


title: Cybergull_CG
---
// Show Maxx and Cybergulls CG. Do not call any character sprites during this time.
<<camera MaxxCG>>
<<fadeIn 2>>
// Play SFX Cybergull Battlecry sound effect
<<playSFX battlecry>>
<<wait 1>>
Luna: <i>I stop my bike at the edge of the shoulder lane, watching as the horde of birds swell before descending upon him and the highway below.</i>
Maxx: No no no no NOOOOO!
Luna: <i>The birds are relentless.</i>
Luna: <i>Pecking, ripping, and ransacking anything that glows, which includes both Maxx and his precious state-of-the-art junkyard motorcycle.</i>
Maxx: Not the face! Not the JAW!! Now the JAWWWWW!!
Luna: <i>I flinch and look away, refusing to watch the gulls tear Maxx’s prized possession and his ego away from him, limb from limb.</i>
Maxx: AHHHHHHHHHHHHRRRRGHHHH!!!
Luna: <i>The cybergulls slowly disperse back into dusk, leaving tokens of their appreciation in the form of noxious droppings spittled across the concrete.</i>
Luna: <i>Whatever is left of Maxx and his motorcycle remains on the highway, like roadkill.</i>
<<fadeOut 2>>
<<stopMusic>>
<<jump BridgeResolution>>
===


title: BridgeResolution
---
// Play Ascension Mellow music track
<<playMusic ascensionMellow>>
<<camera Bridge>>
<<fadeIn 2>>
<<if $withCog == true>>
<<place Luna_Neutral>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
<<place CompanionNubs>>
<<expression CompanionNubs agents>>
<<wait 1>>
Luna: <i>We make it safely to the outskirts of Root Town. I park on the side of the road. Frisscity's lights glitter from the other side of the bridge.</i>
// Play SFX Cybergull M
<<playSFX caws>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
// Enter Cybergull with cog on
<<place CyberSeagull>>
<<expression CyberSeagull cog>>
Luna: <i>The cybergull gang leader descends down from the skies, hovering over my place on the road. The massive cog twinkles in the night sky.</i>
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
Luna: It’s him…
Luna: <i>He watches me carefully through his scarred eye…</i>
<<expression Luna_Neutral shy_annoyed>>
Luna: <i>…Before deciding to poop on me.</i>
Luna: S-Shit!
Luna: <i>Literally. Happy with his revenge, the cybergull departs into the darkness.</i>
// Exit Cybergull
<<pose CyberSeagull SceneSample_CybergullFadeOut>>
<<wait 1>>
<<exit CyberSeagull>>
Luna: Ughhhh, grosssss…!
Luna: (This stuff isn’t gonna come out of my jacket.)
<<exit Luna_Neutral>>
<<exit CompanionNubs>>
<<fadeOut 1>>
<<fadeIn 1>>
<<endif>>
<<place Luna_Neutral>>
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
<<place Nubs>>
<<expression Nubs agents>>
Luna: <i>A sharp noise buzzes from Nubs and I turn to look at him.</i>
<<expression Luna_Neutral surprised>>
<<expression Nubs worried>>
Nubs: H-Huh?
<<expression Luna_Neutral happy>>
Luna: Nubs! You're back!
<<expression Nubs arms_worried>>
Nubs: What happened…?
Luna: Shit. CRAZY shit. And a whole lotta shit. 
<<expression Luna_Neutral neutral>>
Luna: What do you remember?
Nubs: I remember Maxx demanding for my custody. Threatening you with the full force of the AGENTS Legal team and Frisscity police force. And you, driving away with me.
<<expression Nubs wave_worried>>
Nubs: Which is what I don't understand!
<<expression Luna_Neutral arms_neutral>>
Luna: What do you mean?
<<expression Nubs arms_worried>>
Nubs: Why did you decide to take me across The Bridge? To keep me?
Luna: …
<<if $goodend >= 4>>
    <<jump GoodPath>>
<<else>>
    <<jump BadEnding2>>
<<endif>>
===


title: BadEnding2
---
Luna: Delivering you to Root Town was worth a lot on the SL0P app, remember? I have to keep you close if I wanna get paid.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>>
Nubs: Oh…
Luna: And when Maxx cornered me, I knew I’d lose everything. And that’s not an option for me. 
Luna: (I have to survive.)
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
Luna: A job's a job, and I gotta finish it. And to be honest, I don’t think you’re even worth all the trouble I’ve been through tonight.
Nubs: R-Right. This was all just a monetary transaction. Of course…
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedShy>>
Luna: Today's been a huge pain in the ass…
Luna: (And a reminder of how much I hate Frisscity.)
Luna: Let’s just get this over with.
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
// I imagine just the dialogue box, with no sprites appearing
I drive off into Root Town to complete the delivery. The SL0P app tells me to drop off the experiment near Val's corner store, which seems suss at first…
But I don't care. It's not worth my time to think about it right now.
I'm just trying to survive.
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
///////////////////////// Play the Error of Our Ways music track
//////////////////////// Show a screen with THE END text, and an option to Load Game or Return to Title Screen
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
===

